From 30d119ea9d14168510a509cc3c3a35d401497ab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:30:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] rdna-boosts: block 14: qwen4exp support

qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support on the rdna-boosts core, squashed
from the beta/qwen4exp delta (fork qwen4exp tip dd4301fb4, re-based to
the 465e49b9c-era core; promoted to the delivery at the 050dde50c
re-base 2026-09-07):

- QSA layers: fused indexer top-k (GGML_OP_INDEXER_TOPK, radix), sparse
  flash attention (GGML_OP_FLASH_ATTN_QSA) -- the default FA path;
  LLAMA_QSA_SPARSE_FA=0 keeps dense; CPU reference for the sparse op
- fused decode ops GGML_OP_HC_MIX / GGML_OP_HC_COMBINE (+ kernel
  geometry, rms/gamma fold, F32/Q8_0 inject fold, head-call fusion)
- managed lazy reader (llama-lazy-reader.cpp/.h) with PLE n-gram row
  loading and batched cold-page fetch (LLAMA_LAZY_IO_THREADS)
- MTP draft-head support for the Flash-Next GGUFs (--spec-type draft-mtp)
- WS4 hyperconn prefill fusions (DSV4_HC_COMB/PRE/POST); ggml sched
  alloc-fallback sync fix; QSA dense shortcut (DEFAULT ON) + LLAMA_QSA_OFF
- QSA decode campaign (2026-09-07): fused INDEXER_POOL/SCORE ops, f16
  indexer caches, incremental derived block-vector cache, two-round
  16-bit topk select, CUDA device-description gfx-id exposure
- arch policy (2026-09-07 crossover tables): dense decode below the
  per-arch depth, QSA at/above (gfx1151 default 65536);
  LLAMA_QSA_DENSE_DECODE_UNTIL overrides
- MoE weighted-reduction fusion on the Meta-TP path; concat-transposed,
  mmid-512x10, repeat-absorb hc-combine absorb; model support in
  src/models/qwen4exp.cpp

Re-based onto the 050dde50c delivery core 2026-09-07: the only
upstream-drift conflict (ggml-cuda/common.cuh) resolved by keeping both
the upstream gfx90c GCN-APU arch macros and the block's exact-SKU
GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_GFX1151 predicate.  Upstream's branchless Q4_K/Q5_K mmvq
unpack + L2 prefetch and the block's k-quant/decode additions coexist
(mmqq/vecdotq regions disjoint).  Full beta notes + validation:
beta/qwen4exp/README.md.

Amended 2026-09-08 with the compiler-warning cleanup for the
ggml-clang / ggml-clang++ (system clang 16) and ROCm 7.14 HIP builds:
drop the unused n_blocks local in ggml_indexer_fill (ggml.c); add the
GGML_OP_INDEXER_SCORE/GGML_OP_INDEXER_FILL case labels to the CPU
compute-forward switch (GPU-only fused ops; the CPU plan phase already
aborts on them); drop the unreachable break after the noreturn
GGML_ABORT in the HC_MIX/HC_COMBINE CPU type dispatches (ops.cpp);
restore the GGML_CUDA_QSA_INDEXER_CACHE env tri-state (0/1/2) so the
idx_cache == 2 debug probe is actually reachable (was narrowed to bool);
size_t loop counter in the device gfx-id sniff.  No generated-code or
runtime-behavior change in default configs.

Amended 2026-09-08 (2nd) with the qwen4exp tensor-split backend gate:
llm_arch_supports_sm_tensor(qwen4exp) is now true only on HIP builds
(#ifdef GGML_USE_HIP).  The fused QSA/HC/WS4 ops tensor-split through
the meta backend are validated on ROCm only (3x R9700); on backends
that cannot run them on-device (Vulkan, Metal, SYCL) the CPU-fallback
subgraphs leave the meta splitter unable to reconcile mirrored-vs-split
operand states (abort at ggml-backend-meta.cpp handle_generic, e.g. the
qwen4exp gated-attention MUL on Vulkan), and NVIDIA CUDA is untested,
so those builds keep upstream's unsupported (clean error / arch-test
SKIP) instead of crashing.

Amended 2026-09-10: freed-cell KV handling moved from host-side zeroing
to kernel-side masked-V elimination, and the earlier host zeroing
(seq_rm/seq_keep/clear per-free memsets, 2026-09-09 fold of the strix
aad5adb08f port) is REMOVED.  The llama-kv-cache files are back to the
upstream state (no zero_freed/rows_hw/sharers wiring; evicting a KV
sequence is pure host cell bookkeeping again on every backend).  In its
place block 14 now carries the three kernel fixes that make freed-cell
content unreadable in masked flash attention, so the host workaround is
unnecessary:

- HIP fattn-tile.cuh: in the packed-bf16 PV path, zero the per-warp V
  register copies of rows whose P is exactly +0.0 across the warp's
  columns (the fully-masked rows) before the bf16 dot.
- HIP fattn-mma-f16.cuh: after each V-tile slice is staged in shared
  memory, zero the rows the mask tile marks blocked (-inf) for every
  query column of the block; one extra uniform barrier on the masked
  path (ncols2 > 1 || mask_h) only; compile-time excluded for the
  V_is_K_view and NVIDIA swizzled (swz_V) paths.
- Vulkan flash_attn_cm1.comp: never read V of fully masked columns
  (per-column liveness -> V of dead columns stays +0.0); flash_attn.comp
  scalar path likewise skips the V load for dead columns.

All three are unconditional in their kernel paths (no arch/env gating):
they are correctness fixes for any masked flash-attention column whose
cell is stale/freed (batch serving, KV eviction), active by default on
every device.  They were root-caused and validated on the Strix Halo
box (single gfx1151): 16/16 identical-request determinism gates pass on
both ROCm and Vulkan with the host zeroing disabled, bit-identical
across every KV cache type each backend's FA supports (ROCm
f16/bf16/q8_0/q4_0; Vulkan also q4_1/q5_0/q5_1/iq4_nl), with
test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_EXT vs CPU 4591/4591 (ROCm) and 7822/7822
(Vulkan) and no measurable decode/prefill regression (tg128 within
0.05% at depth-16384; pp within single-run drift).  Full record:
wip/strix-halo/kvzero/RECORD-2026-09-09.md and
wip/kv-sign-leak/HANDOVER-2026-09-09-mma-f16.md in the delivery repo.
The 2026-09-09 amendment text below is retained as history only; the
freed-cell zeroing gate it describes no longer exists in the block.
